To align the caption of a table left in LaTeX without using the `caption` package, you can use the `\captionsetup` command from the `caption` package, even if you don't load the entire package. Here's how you can do it:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{caption}

\begin{document}

\begin{table}
  \captionsetup{justification=raggedright}
  \caption{This is a table caption aligned to the left.}
  \begin{tabular}{cc}
    Column 1 & Column 2 \\
    Value 1 & Value 2 \\
    Value 3 & Value 4 \\
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

\end{document}
```

In this example, the `\captionsetup{justification=raggedright}` line aligns the caption to the left. You can also use `justification=left` to achieve the same effect.

If you don't want to use the `caption` package at all, you can manually set the caption alignment using the `\caption` command:

```latex
\documentclass{article}

\begin{document}

\begin{table}
  \caption{\raggedright This is a table caption aligned to the left.}
  \begin{tabular}{cc}
    Column 1 & Column 2 \\
    Value 1 & Value 2 \\
    Value 3 & Value 4 \\
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

\end{document}
```

In this case, the `\raggedright` command is used to align the caption to the left.

